WEBVTT

00:06.970 --> 00:09.805
An aspiring serenade of instincts!

00:09.806 --> 00:12.640
Seijakusa wo ima uchikowasu
yaketsuku honnou no sere naade

00:12.930 --> 00:18.150
- Just once is alright, I want to tell you about the blooming impact!
- Ichido de iikara tsutaetai saki tagaru shou geki wo

00:20.230 --> 00:23.630
- Yeah! Light Now, Scream now! Break the breaks!
- YEAH! Light now scream now bukkowase bureeki wa

00:23.940 --> 00:25.250
- Wind speed is freedom, get on!
- Fuusoku wa freedom norikomi na

00:25.260 --> 00:26.780
- Mind style is E.G.O!
- Mind style wa E.G.O

00:26.783 --> 00:29.290
- Hiding the city's passing whispers
- Ikizuki machi koe wo hisome

00:29.370 --> 00:30.850
Seeking my presence.

00:30.851 --> 00:32.330
Boku no sonzai wo motomeru

00:32.750 --> 00:35.370
- The things you want to protect...
- Mamoritai mono wa itsudatte

00:35.460 --> 00:38.330
- Can never be protected.
- Mamorenai koto wa bakari darou

00:38.340 --> 00:41.860
I know how much I'm worth cannot be
changed but there's no reason to be swayed.

00:41.861 --> 00:45.380
Sadamerareta kachikan ni
boku wo furuwasu imi nado nai yo

00:46.430 --> 00:49.270
I don't mind if I get hurt
because you gave me a miracle.

00:49.271 --> 00:52.110
Kizutsuitemo katawanai
kiseki wo kimi ga kureta kara

00:52.430 --> 00:56.890
- Just once is alright, I want to tell you, we're winders!
- Ichido de iikara tsutaetai, bokutachi ga WINDER

00:57.150 --> 01:00.130
- If you choose to silently struggle against
who you are - Arisou de nai jibun rashisa ni

01:00.133 --> 01:03.030
- That seems to be there but is not.
- Koe mo dasezu mogakuno nara

01:03.033 --> 01:06.010
- You probably should go to the self centered tomorrow
I told you about - Shi no go no iu, katte na ashita ni

01:06.050 --> 01:07.135
And...

01:07.136 --> 01:08.220
sakasete mita yo

01:08.280 --> 01:10.180
The reality in your heart.

01:10.181 --> 01:12.080
Kokoro no riaru

01:14.500 --> 01:16.310
I am right here.

01:16.311 --> 01:18.120
Boku wa kokoni iru

01:21.520 --> 01:24.180
- I want to flip light and darkness around, victorious return of the world.
- Hikari to kage tokkae WORLD he gaisen

01:24.380 --> 01:27.470
- Now, the will to go towards the future and play on!
- Saa WILL TO GO mirai he to PLAY ON!

01:34.150 --> 01:36.219
Good morning, everyone.

01:36.220 --> 01:37.910
Today is Sunday.

01:40.180 --> 01:43.080
Of course, school is out,

01:44.320 --> 01:46.790
but I still came to school.

01:55.250 --> 01:56.880
Of course, there's no one at school.

02:03.890 --> 02:05.990
It's very, very quiet.

02:10.640 --> 02:11.640
Club activity.

02:12.640 --> 02:15.270
This must be the blue spring.

02:19.350 --> 02:20.780
Good mor-

02:33.710 --> 02:38.760
O-on a Sunday morning,

02:39.880 --> 02:41.700
Stop it.

02:42.210 --> 02:43.490
Stay still and don't move.

02:55.570 --> 02:58.329
N-no! It's not like that, Shinozaki-kun!

02:58.330 --> 03:00.679
It's not the kind of weird
thing you're thinking!

03:00.680 --> 03:03.239
I don't want to hear any excuses.

03:03.240 --> 03:05.849
No. It's not an excuse.

03:05.850 --> 03:08.250
Don't worry, Terao-san.

03:08.680 --> 03:12.090
My good point is that
I'm a tight-lipped man,

03:12.600 --> 03:14.630
and something like this,

03:15.320 --> 03:18.309
I won't let anyone know this secret.

03:18.310 --> 03:20.259
No! I just said it's not like that.

03:20.260 --> 03:22.450
That was for bicycling.

03:24.930 --> 03:25.930
Earthquake?

03:26.280 --> 03:27.800
Terao-san! It's an earthquake!

03:32.000 --> 03:33.000
You-Yousuke!

03:36.820 --> 03:42.229
Umm... What do you mean
"That was for bicycling"?

03:42.230 --> 03:44.560
Every cyclist does this.

03:51.190 --> 03:52.330
But, why?

03:52.770 --> 03:58.450
See, at times when you fall, pebbles can get stuck
in the skin which can prolong the time of heal.

03:59.040 --> 04:00.939
If leg hair also got stuck in it,
then that would be bad as well.

04:00.940 --> 04:03.340
Stuck into the skin? No!

04:03.790 --> 04:07.129
But, it's not good to
fear falling too much.

04:07.130 --> 04:11.519
There are some who say that the more times
a road racer falls, the faster he becomes,

04:11.520 --> 04:13.320
especially on downward slopes.

04:14.840 --> 04:16.770
The more times one falls?

04:17.210 --> 04:18.210
Yep.

04:18.960 --> 04:20.360
Can become faster?

04:28.260 --> 04:31.200
Th-Then... I'll shave my leg, too.

04:36.950 --> 04:37.950
Really?

04:38.890 --> 04:40.670
Then, let me help you.

04:41.240 --> 04:43.990
N-no n-need. I'll do it myself.

04:54.270 --> 04:57.060
There wasn't a need to
shave the hair down there, too.

04:57.810 --> 05:01.969
A-are you all right, Shinozaki-kun?
It'll grow back in no time.

05:01.970 --> 05:03.669
Will it?

05:03.670 --> 05:04.760
Yousuke!

05:07.210 --> 05:09.230
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

05:21.600 --> 05:23.059
We've kept you waiting.

05:23.060 --> 05:24.900
You're early, Yuki.

05:25.980 --> 05:27.830
I'm never late when it's time to play.

05:30.450 --> 05:33.470
O yeah,

05:34.330 --> 05:35.610
Did you do five sets?

05:36.730 --> 05:44.730
Let's see... Umm... I only counted to twelve sets. If I counted
those after eating dinner... Umm... I can't remember at all.

05:47.150 --> 05:51.629
Umm... And yesterday, I also
secretly went to ride the bicycle.

05:51.630 --> 05:53.329
Ama-amazing!

05:53.330 --> 05:57.039
That's awesome!

05:57.040 --> 06:00.250
N-no. Is that so?

06:00.790 --> 06:02.529
You're still far off, kid.

06:02.530 --> 06:04.460
When I started off, I could do thirty sets.

06:04.840 --> 06:05.960
Still far off...

06:06.500 --> 06:08.969
That's why I said, most people
can't reach that kind of level.

06:08.970 --> 06:10.180
It's nothing...

06:10.960 --> 06:11.930
You're still far, far off.

06:11.931 --> 06:13.609
Still far off...

06:13.610 --> 06:15.679
He's definitely amazing.

06:15.680 --> 06:16.930
I'm more amazing.

06:17.490 --> 06:18.969
Isn't he amazing?

06:18.970 --> 06:21.039
I'm far more amazing than him.

06:21.040 --> 06:22.389
You're not honest at all.

06:22.390 --> 06:23.899
No! I'm the one who's amazing.

06:23.900 --> 06:25.519
You're impossible!

06:25.520 --> 06:27.239
Idiot. You just realized that now?

06:27.240 --> 06:28.860
Right. I am stupid.

06:29.270 --> 06:32.050
Then, today, I will
openly ride the bicycle.

06:33.020 --> 06:36.149
Hold it.

06:36.150 --> 06:40.000
But, he said I was amazing...

06:40.640 --> 06:44.210
Shut up. You still have a lot to do.

06:48.160 --> 06:50.280
I can't! I can't!

06:53.790 --> 06:57.829
Yo-Yousuke-san, this I definitely can't.

06:57.830 --> 07:00.770
I'm willing to eat carrots, to
never leave green peppers...

07:03.110 --> 07:04.140
Really?

07:05.350 --> 07:06.690
I swear to God.

07:10.210 --> 07:11.450
Wait!

07:12.640 --> 07:16.540
This is the main point.

07:17.450 --> 07:19.700
I can't. I definitely can't.

07:26.020 --> 07:29.420
Listen,

07:30.020 --> 07:32.859
even top racers can tell
without seeing you ride a bicycle.

07:32.860 --> 07:34.580
You must first establish a good foundation.

07:34.620 --> 07:37.809
It's important to strengthen other
pars of the body than the bicycle ones.

07:37.810 --> 07:40.140
So for today, swim.

07:43.980 --> 07:46.740
I... I can't swim.

07:47.170 --> 07:48.519
‌‌ ‌‌

07:48.520 --> 07:53.240
Shinozaki's wounds from the last
time he fell haven't healed completely.

07:53.680 --> 07:56.689
Is Yousuke worried that
it'll be a burden on his legs?

07:56.690 --> 07:57.690
What?

07:57.730 --> 08:00.700
No, no, no.

08:02.320 --> 08:03.660
Terao Kouichi -

08:05.340 --> 08:07.609
It hurts, Yousuke!

08:07.610 --> 08:10.420
Come! You're too soft on that kid.

08:32.250 --> 08:34.300
Will Shinozaki-kun be okay?

08:34.820 --> 08:36.939
Although Yousuke told me not to interfere,

08:36.940 --> 08:42.810
he has already experienced a taste
of the fear that's impossible to control.

08:51.040 --> 08:53.840
Hey,

08:55.870 --> 08:58.800
A floating corpse?!

09:00.140 --> 09:03.000
I feel like Yousuke-san hates me.

09:03.930 --> 09:05.200
Why?

09:05.740 --> 09:07.149
Isn't it because

09:07.150 --> 09:09.229
Isn't it because he
thinks I'm holding him up?

09:09.230 --> 09:14.269
Even though Terao-san
takes good care of me,

09:14.270 --> 09:15.929
and wears clothes like a bad guy.

09:15.930 --> 09:18.879
T-the clothes and his attitude
have nothing to do with that.

09:18.880 --> 09:21.990
And,

09:25.420 --> 09:29.370
Shinozaki-kun,

09:30.530 --> 09:31.980
Think back.

09:33.590 --> 09:37.430
Umm...

09:37.970 --> 09:39.890
Yep, that. Yousuke.

09:43.390 --> 09:48.850
The bicycle and the body must be compatible
in order to fully bring out your strength.

09:49.740 --> 09:53.320
To be compatible,

09:54.080 --> 09:58.530
Yousuke stays late every night,
by himself, to adjust the bicycles.

10:14.930 --> 10:19.880
When you joined the club, the
happiest person here was Yousuke.

10:25.110 --> 10:28.950
Yousuke is a very famous
person in the bicycling world.

11:06.200 --> 11:09.230
He's known as the "Uncrowned King".

11:17.400 --> 11:19.900
The Uncrowned King.

11:20.520 --> 11:24.160
Road Racing isn't a one-person battle.

11:25.320 --> 11:28.680
Actually, the most important thing
about bicycling is the teamwork,

11:29.840 --> 11:31.680
because one must have
outstanding assistants.

11:32.570 --> 11:34.680
One must have outstanding assistants?

11:35.510 --> 11:36.710
So the ace can win.

11:37.460 --> 11:39.040
So the ace can win.

11:48.170 --> 11:53.360
Although Yousuke has a
bad attitude, he's just like that:

11:53.880 --> 11:56.150
neither giving not willing.

11:56.920 --> 12:01.530
Even though his individual
strength is strong, he rarely wins.

12:03.150 --> 12:06.570
Because there aren't many
who can keep up with him.

12:07.610 --> 12:10.160
In the end, his companions all left him.

12:10.830 --> 12:12.650
This is a genius' loneliness.

12:13.480 --> 12:15.200
But, that's that.

12:36.340 --> 12:38.150
Un-Un-Un... Uncrowned King.

12:39.320 --> 12:42.029
The Uncrowned King. So cool!

12:42.030 --> 12:44.569
T-that's all you noticed...

12:44.570 --> 12:47.620
Terao-san. I'll work hard!

12:48.140 --> 12:51.019
Being anticipated by the Uncrowned King,

12:51.020 --> 12:53.849
I'll work hard!

12:56.850 --> 12:59.579
Save me.

12:59.580 --> 13:00.629
Shinozaki-kun.

13:00.630 --> 13:03.050
Terao-san, lend a hand... A hand...

13:18.860 --> 13:19.860
How is it?

13:20.470 --> 13:23.610
Miss, that's the back.

13:33.760 --> 13:35.410
Violence!

13:37.820 --> 13:40.590
I'll... Work hard, too.

13:41.610 --> 13:45.339
I definitely... Won't let
Yousuke-san's hope... Down.

13:45.340 --> 13:48.299
I'll work hard, too. I
definitely won't... Yousuke...

13:51.090 --> 13:52.090
Keep it up!

13:53.110 --> 13:55.459
Keep it up! There's only two minutes left!

13:55.460 --> 13:57.520
As ‌‌long as the whole
team catches up, we'll win!

13:58.160 --> 14:00.729
It's impossible, You-chan.

14:00.730 --> 14:02.440
I'm already tired.

14:04.320 --> 14:06.150
Fine. I'll get the championship by myself.

14:13.240 --> 14:14.790
Damn it!

14:15.520 --> 14:16.969
Damn! Damn!

14:16.970 --> 14:20.840
Why? Am I stronger than those guys!

14:21.670 --> 14:23.679
Why didn't you catch up?

14:23.680 --> 14:25.600
Don't you guys want to win?

14:26.480 --> 14:28.220
Fukazawa-kun, you're too stubborn.

14:28.690 --> 14:31.849
Obviously it's you who doesn't have
any sense of teamwork, You-chan.

14:31.850 --> 14:36.029
The coach said that finishing the race
is more important than winning the race.

14:36.030 --> 14:38.790
I don't want to ride with Fukazawa.

14:44.680 --> 14:48.400
Fine.

14:55.510 --> 14:56.670
Don't follow me.

14:58.700 --> 15:00.339
I quit, too.

15:00.340 --> 15:02.520
I told you not to follow me.

15:03.130 --> 15:04.130
Why?

15:04.300 --> 15:05.540
No reason.

15:06.520 --> 15:07.840
Is it because I ride slow?

15:08.480 --> 15:09.550
You're not slow.

15:11.090 --> 15:12.530
Just slower than me.

15:14.110 --> 15:15.890
I'll tell you, Kouichi.

15:17.930 --> 15:21.520
My dream is to become the Japanese
Champion in the Tour de France.

15:24.040 --> 15:25.909
Sorry, You-chan.

15:25.910 --> 15:28.279
If only I was faster...

15:28.280 --> 15:30.059
If I was a bit stronger...

15:30.060 --> 15:33.810
Idiot! Didn't I say you're not slow?

15:36.610 --> 15:39.410
Don't cry all of a sudden!

15:41.840 --> 15:44.250
Sorry,

15:45.130 --> 15:46.710
I couldn't help you.

15:59.590 --> 16:01.230
My hands are too small.

16:07.850 --> 16:10.530
I'm not working hard enough...

16:12.130 --> 16:13.470
My strength is not enough...

16:15.200 --> 16:17.120
My knowledge is not enough...

16:35.870 --> 16:37.200
So many wounds.

16:37.770 --> 16:42.270
There are some who say that the more times
a road racer falls, the faster he becomes.

16:43.760 --> 16:45.979
This isn't talent bestowed by the heavens,

16:45.980 --> 16:49.250
but strength gained through
hard work and lots of training.

16:53.150 --> 16:54.150
What?

16:54.350 --> 16:55.540
Nothing.

16:56.900 --> 17:01.760
Yousuke was the happiest person
here, when you joined the club.

17:05.610 --> 17:08.960
My hands are too small.

17:11.120 --> 17:15.800
I... I will one day answer your hopes.

17:22.820 --> 17:24.899
I'll take my leave first.

17:24.900 --> 17:26.060
Good work.

17:32.380 --> 17:33.530
What's with that guy?

17:34.700 --> 17:37.740
The "fire" is lit all right, by someone.

17:41.740 --> 17:43.909
Are you somewhat happy Yousuke?

17:43.910 --> 17:44.939
Idiot.

17:44.940 --> 17:46.969
Yuki-chan sure brought over a nice kid.

17:46.970 --> 17:48.239
Really?

17:48.240 --> 17:50.080
We'll become a good team.

17:50.880 --> 17:51.899
Kouichi.

17:53.640 --> 17:54.809
It hurts!

17:54.810 --> 17:56.859
Where did you go ans slack off just then?

17:56.860 --> 17:58.279
St-stop it, You-chan.

17:58.280 --> 18:00.030
Don't call me "You-chan".

18:04.600 --> 18:09.810
These wounds...

18:14.190 --> 18:17.019
That was fun, fun.

18:17.020 --> 18:19.559
Then, let's keep playing!

18:29.520 --> 18:32.179
Are these idiots still practicing?

18:32.180 --> 18:33.579
Yuki?

18:33.580 --> 18:34.710
I'm coming.

18:42.160 --> 18:46.669
Shi-Shi-Shi-Shi-Shi-Shi-Shinozaki-kun!

18:46.670 --> 18:48.110
So stupid.

19:00.696 --> 19:01.740
Turned into a fish.

19:10.280 --> 19:11.580
I'm home.

19:14.790 --> 19:18.170
Kouichi, sorry. I went to your mother's
place. Please look after the store. Dad

19:21.860 --> 19:25.930
Terao Kouichi, six years old.

19:51.960 --> 19:57.250
No one comes to this
broken, old store, anyway.

19:59.040 --> 20:01.090
I hate bicycles.

20:08.490 --> 20:11.020
Wh-wh-what was that?

20:18.100 --> 20:19.100
Please.

20:30.510 --> 20:32.000
Hey, I say...

20:33.410 --> 20:38.089
This isn't a hospital. This is just a broken,
old bicycle shop on the corner of the city.

20:38.090 --> 20:42.720
If you enter here covered with blood,
it's rather troublesome, understand?

20:43.930 --> 20:45.680
I was hit by this at the time.

20:46.460 --> 20:48.520
I'll catch it to pay for the bicycle's fee.

20:56.700 --> 20:58.060
What a weird bicycle.

21:01.060 --> 21:05.199
What?

21:05.200 --> 21:07.429
And you even put on some blood.

21:07.430 --> 21:10.549
What is that bicycle? An antique?

21:10.550 --> 21:16.350
Well, my old man's not here. If it's fixing
the bicycle, then go somewhere else. Good-bye.

21:17.480 --> 21:22.150
What? As the bicycle store owner's
son, you don't know how to fix it?

21:23.670 --> 21:26.860
Stay where you are, you bastard!

21:43.420 --> 21:46.139
Yuki, where did the guy who hit me go?

21:46.140 --> 21:47.510
He just got stopped.

21:48.340 --> 21:49.340
Let's go buy candy.

21:51.330 --> 21:57.530
That bastard. You better
remember this, you weird person.

21:58.740 --> 22:01.349
Terao Kouichi and Fukazawa Yousuke,

22:01.350 --> 22:04.490
three months later, became a team.

22:07.900 --> 22:10.295
Kaze ga toorisugiteku

22:10.296 --> 22:12.690
The wind glides by,

22:13.280 --> 22:15.240
Karada wo surinukete

22:15.241 --> 22:17.200
Brushing against our body.

22:17.530 --> 22:20.260
Itsushika iro ase bokete shimatta

22:20.261 --> 22:22.990
The colors faded in the
farthest end of the sky,

22:23.040 --> 22:25.080
Sora no saihate de

22:25.081 --> 22:27.120
before we realized.

22:28.170 --> 22:32.170
Nama atatakai kaze ga fuiteru fuiteru

22:32.171 --> 22:36.170
The luke warm breeze is blowing, blowing.

22:37.800 --> 22:39.700
Mujun darake no sekai de

22:39.701 --> 22:41.600
In a world full on inconsistency,

22:41.720 --> 22:44.575
Toke sou no kimi ga
futto boku ni waraikaketa

22:44.576 --> 22:47.430
Melting into it, you
grin at me with a whiff.

22:56.360 --> 22:58.655
Kaze ga toorisugiteku

22:58.656 --> 23:00.950
The wind glides by,

23:01.200 --> 23:03.015
Karada wo surinukete

23:03.016 --> 23:04.830
Brushing against our body.

23:05.410 --> 23:08.165
Itsushika a iro ase bokete shimatta

23:08.166 --> 23:10.920
The colors faded before we realized.

23:11.000 --> 23:15.565
Sora no saihate de aou

23:15.566 --> 23:20.130
Let's meet at the furthest end of the sky.

23:36.780 --> 23:38.719
Good afternoon. This is Shinozaki.

23:38.720 --> 23:41.549
Does everyone know Fukazawa Hill?

23:41.550 --> 23:44.039
It's actually named after Yousuke-san.

23:44.040 --> 23:45.269
It's amazing!

23:45.270 --> 23:49.100
One day, I also want
something named after me.
